findings.description:
`testRecoveryKeysSetupAndLogin` does one setup and one successful login. The provider's `isValid` (`BackwardsCompatibilityUserStorage.java:326-340`) accepts any stored code with `anyMatch` and never consumes one. `getCredentials` rebuilds the model from the full list each time, so the form always asks for code #1.

Untested as a result:
- rejection of an invalid code for a federated user;
- code consumption and progression to the next code;
- the exhausted-codes branch at `RecoveryAuthnCodesFormAuthenticator.java:85-92`, where the first finding sits;
- the fallback to local storage when the user storage declines the update (`CredentialHelper.java:128-130`);
- the `.or(...)` fallback in `RecoveryAuthnCodesUtils.getCredential`.

The class Javadoc (lines 59-62) says the provider mirrors a 4.8.3 implementation and should not need changes in later versions. The diff contradicts that in three ways:

- it adds a `getCredentials` override, an SPI method that did not exist in 4.8.3;
- it uses `RecoveryAuthnCodesCredentialModel`;
- it assigns an ID to the OTP credential (line 179) and returns OTP from `getCredentials` (lines 247-249).

The OTP change is not limited to the new feature. OTP deletion for this provider can now match the federated-ID branch at `CredentialDeleteHelper.java:63-70` instead of the legacy `"-id"` branch at lines 75-80. I did not trace which ID the account REST returns, so whether the existing OTP tests still exercise the legacy branch is unconfirmed. A separate test provider for federated recovery codes would keep this one true to its purpose; otherwise update the Javadoc.
